### Register (201). Copy accessToken into http-client.env.json as "token".
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "budi@example.com", "password": "Passw0rdOk", "displayName": "Budi", "deviceName": "dev" }

### Login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "budi@example.com", "password": "Passw0rdOk", "deviceName": "dev" }

### Refresh (rotates the refresh token; the old one stops working)
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "paste refreshToken" }

### Logout this device -> 204
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "paste refreshToken" }

### Me
GET {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update me
PATCH {{host}}/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "displayName": "Budi S", "defaultCurrency": "IDR" }

### Forgot password -> always 204 (in dev the link is written to the server log)
POST {{host}}/auth/password/forgot
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "budi@example.com" }

### Reset with the token from the link (single use, 30 min) -> 204, signs out every device
POST {{host}}/auth/password/reset
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "paste token", "newPassword": "NewPassw0rd" }

### Verify the email with the token from the sign-up link (public) -> { email, creditsGranted }
POST {{host}}/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "paste token" }

### Send a new verification link (voids the older one) -> 204
POST {{host}}/auth/email/resend
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
